# Secrets for a telegram-agent-estate instance.
#
# Install to the path named by `telegram.token_file` in the instance config —
# by convention ~/.config/<instance-name>/env — and `chmod 600` it.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ONLY PLACE THE BOT TOKEN MAY LIVE. Specifically, it must NOT
# appear in:
#   - the launchd plist's EnvironmentVariables
#   - the repo (any repo)
#   - a turn's environment
# Reason, concretely: the official telegram channel plugin is enabled at user
# scope, so it loads inside every `claude` session including the headless turns
# this stack spawns. It starts polling any TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN it can find, which
# means a leaked token turns every turn into a second poller that 409-wars the
# instance's own receiver. The estate reads this file directly instead.

TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Optional, per instance: any API keys this instance's MCP servers or scripts
# need. Add each variable's NAME to `env_passthrough:` in the instance config,
# or the runner's environment sanitizer will (correctly) withhold it from turns.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY MUST NOT BE SET. Turns bill to the subscription via the
# keychain OAuth credential; an API key here would move billing to metered API
# credits. The runner drops it unconditionally, so setting it here does nothing
# except confuse the next reader.
